ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":136,"prev":138,"next":140,"titles":143,"firmware":55},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":12,"order":13,"path":14,"context":15,"summary":20,"status":21,"firmware":22,"facts":28,"procedures":79,"parameters":103,"related":104,"body":118,"sources":119,"official_url":32,"controls":131},"instrument.engine","Engine page and changing engine (M1)",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11],"engine page","engine list","change engine","choose engine","sound source","synth engines","load an engine","instrument",10,"knowledge/manual/units/instrument/engine.md",{"modes":16,"screens":17},[12],[18,19],"M1","preset browser","`M1` is the engine page: its encoders edit the loaded engine's own parameters. `shift + M1` brings up the preset browser (by engine on OS 1.1.33, by category on OS 1.2: click `E1` for the engines), and loading one of an engine's presets changes the engine and the whole sound.","current",{"min":23,"changed_in":24,"guide_version":26,"verified_on":27},"1.0.9",[25],"1.2.0","1.1.15",null,[29,34,38,42,46,51,57,61,65,68,71,74],{"id":30,"text":31,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"m1-controls","On `M1` the four encoders edit the loaded engine's own parameters, so what each one does depends on the engine.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/instrument#engine","official",{"id":35,"text":36,"source":37,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"synths","There are eight synth engines — axis, dissolve, epiano, hardsync, organ, prism, simple and wavetable — each with its own character.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/synth-engines",{"id":39,"text":40,"source":41,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"samplers","Three sampler engines play recorded audio — the synth sampler, the drum sampler and the multisampler.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/sample",{"id":43,"text":44,"source":45,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"midi","The midi engine makes no sound of its own; it turns the track into a MIDI sequencer for external gear and uses `M2` and `M3` for CC controls.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/synth-engines#external",{"id":47,"text":48,"source":49,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":50},"list","Twelve engines in all — the eight synths, the three samplers and midi.","docs/research/20-midi-control.md#21-the-16-tracks-and-their-default-channels","derived",{"id":52,"text":53,"source":54,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":55,"confidence":56},"midi-ccs","Over MIDI, CC12–15 on the track's channel move the four `M1` parameters of every synth engine; the drum sampler, synth sampler and multisampler pages ignore them.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#3-midi-reach-on-1133-verified-on-screen","1.1.33","verified",{"id":58,"text":59,"source":60,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":55,"confidence":56},"top-bar","A synth engine page lists its four values in a top bar — coloured cells on prism, epiano and wavetable, plain text on simple and axis, none on organ — above a picture drawn from the four values; prism, dissolve and hardsync animate while notes sound, organ's drawbars glide to new values and wavetable's drift keeps its copies turning.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#21-general",{"id":62,"text":63,"source":64,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":55,"confidence":56},"browser","On OS 1.1.33 there is no separate engine list; `shift + M1` brings up the preset browser on the track's current preset — the track number over the word preset at the left, the engines in the middle with the track's engine boxed, and that engine's presets on the right.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#26-preset-browser-shift--m1",{"id":66,"text":67,"source":64,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":55,"confidence":56},"browser-engines","On a unit running OS 1.1.33 it listed eleven engines, alphabetically (axis, dissolve, drum, epiano, hardsync, multisampler, organ, prism, sampler, simple, wavetable) and no midi engine; how OS 1.1.33 puts an instrument track on midi is still open, and this app's replica lists midi last.",{"id":69,"text":70,"source":64,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":55,"confidence":56},"load-changes-engine","Turning `E1` to an engine highlights its first preset; loading a preset changes the engine with the whole sound (all four pages) and returns to the track's `M1` page.",{"id":72,"text":73,"source":64,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":55,"confidence":56},"e1-click","In the browser a click of `E1` swaps between by engine and by category (a popup says which) instead of confirming, as it did in the older engine list the guide describes.",{"id":75,"text":76,"source":77,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":27,"confidence":78},"browser-os12","On OS 1.2 the browser that `shift + M1` brings up opens by category, so changing engine starts with a click of `E1` to the engine view; the engine list there also holds drumline, a thirteenth engine that arrived with OS 1.2.","docs/research/81-os12-tutorial-replay-beginner.md#5-differences-most-noticeable-first-video-seconds-b-behaviour-s-screen-a-sound","community-verified",[80],{"id":81,"goal":82,"preconditions":83,"steps":86,"result":102,"source":64,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":55,"confidence":56},"choose","Change the engine of the selected instrument track",[84,85],"instrument mode","the track is selected",[87,90,93,96,99],{"keys":88,"note":89,"set":27},"shift + M1","the preset browser opens on the track's preset",{"keys":91,"note":92,"set":27},"click E1","only if it lists categories, as OS 1.2 does on opening (OS 1.1.33 opens by engine); a click swaps to by engine",{"keys":94,"note":95,"set":27},"turn E1","highlight an engine; its first preset is highlighted",{"keys":97,"note":98,"set":27},"turn E2","optional; another of its presets",{"keys":100,"note":101,"set":27},"click E2","loads it","The track runs the new engine with that preset's sound, and `M1` shows the engine's parameters.",[],[105,106,107,108,109,110,111,112,113,114,115,116,117],"instrume